83
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:27,300
Ridiculous.

84
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,800
So utterly, pathetically ridiculous!

85
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,130
I can't even stand to look at you anymore!

86
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:36,650
This is the height of stupidity, Emiya Shirou!

87
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,610
You'll become a champion of justice?

88
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:42,050
Being right isn't everything?

89
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:45,740
Given what you now know, why can't you see that you're mistaken?

90
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:49,460
Justice is a representation of order.

91
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:53,020
Saving one and saving all are two different things.

92
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:56,000
They are mutually exclusive!

93
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,800
The more you strive for proper salvation,

94
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,410
the more you'll be consumed by your own contradiction.

95
00:01:03,010 --> 00:01:04,880
You'll end up a simple killer for hire!

96
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:09,470
If you're unable to see that, then die.

97
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:11,890
Be smashed to pieces, along with your ideals!

98
00:01:11,890 --> 00:01:14,310
Burn out before you can achieve anything!

99
00:01:14,310 --> 00:01:19,080
Yes, if that happened, my erroneous existence would vanish like mist.

100
00:01:19,770 --> 00:01:21,940
I'll wipe out any trace that you ever existed...

101
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:25,780
with my own two hands!

102
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:29,970
They're starting to overlap.

103
00:01:31,070 --> 00:01:34,580
If this continues, Shirou is certain to catch up to him.

104
00:01:35,490 --> 00:01:36,380
However...

