5323
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:44,880
You little...

5324
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:55,340
Why am I even bothering to fight him fairly?

5325
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:57,810
If I took a few steps back, this would all be over.

5326
00:03:57,810 --> 00:04:00,440
But something tells me that if I took even one step back,

5327
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:03,520
it would mean admitting my defeat in a crucial aspect!

5328
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:06,480
No, this is all but over.

5329
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:12,020
He's already dead on his feet.

5330
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:13,360
This is the final...

5331
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:20,330
Am I stupid? How many times will I seemingly land the final blow before I learn my lesson?

5332
00:04:20,910 --> 00:04:22,740
He won't stay down.

5333
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:24,470
He won't reach his limit.

5334
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:28,320
He's long since gone past it.

5335
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:35,590
And that's because the thing he's attempting to cut down stopped being me long ago.

5336
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:37,600
I know it...

5337
00:04:38,410 --> 00:04:41,930
I know that haggard look all too well!

5338
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:43,980
I know all too well...

5339
00:04:44,690 --> 00:04:49,870
the man with an indomitable spirit who was never defeated, who never gave up.

5340
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:58,550
The cruel embodiment of justice who struggled toward his ideal of saving all, even as it was shared by none...

5341
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,950
I know that ugly sight all too well!

5342
00:05:04,250 --> 00:05:10,300
The idea that perhaps it is possible to save all who suffer...

5343
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:14,300
I know that sinful manner of living all too well!

5344
00:05:32,470 --> 00:05:37,350
What Shirou is trying to cut down is the self that stands in his way.

5345
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:42,180
To remain true to what he's believed in—
what he will continue believing in.

5346
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:49,540
What Archer is trying to kill is the self that gave rise to him.

5347
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:53,180
To wipe out the mistakes he is doomed to repeat in the future.

5348
00:05:56,410 --> 00:05:58,970
Once, they had a dream.

5349
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:06,190
Both were right.

5350
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,730
Both of them were right.

5351
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:13,950
It's just that the outcome was not what they wished for.

5352
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,740
Even if nothing but regrets remained,

5353
00:06:19,230 --> 00:06:23,290
if they were able to achieve many of their ideals in the process, then...

5354
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:32,860
That figure, knowing he cannot win, knowing it is meaningless,

5355
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:35,380
yet continuing to fight all the same...

5356
00:06:36,150 --> 00:06:39,260
That symbolizes the very mistakes I made.

5357
00:06:39,770 --> 00:06:42,430
Why am I...

5358
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:48,270
No, the result will be the same.

5359
00:06:48,270 --> 00:06:52,150
You'll lose all hope, just as I have!

5360
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,290
How ironic.

5361
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:04,510
Your mana gave out before your spirit did?

5362
00:07:05,170 --> 00:07:07,790
That blade is the only weapon left to you.

5363
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:13,130
In any event, Emiya Shirou's battle ends here!

5364
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:17,610
Yeah, you're right.

5365
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:19,500
My wish is a fake.

5366
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:23,900
But I found it beautiful.

5367
00:07:25,470 --> 00:07:29,720
I understand that putting others before myself is hypocritical.

5368
00:07:30,470 --> 00:07:31,600
But even so...

5369
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:37,470
Even so, the thought of being able to live like that inspired me.

5370
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:40,590
Even if my life is a sham,

5371
00:07:40,590 --> 00:07:45,660
the wish for others to be happy is still beautiful.

5372
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,910
I won't lose anything.

5373
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:52,030
Even if I'm being foolish, I won't turn back.

5374
00:07:52,550 --> 00:07:55,000
I know my dream isn't...

5375
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,750
Even if I'm a fake to the very end,

5376
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:01,580
I know my dream isn't a mistake!

5377
00:08:09,150 --> 00:08:10,270
Begone!

5378
00:08:18,410 --> 00:08:19,480
It's not...

5379
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,400
It's not...

5380
00:08:24,950 --> 00:08:26,030
My dream...

5381
00:08:26,910 --> 00:08:28,740
isn't a mistake!

5382
00:08:44,850 --> 00:08:47,100
I'll do it for you.

5383
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:50,450
Just leave...

5384
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:54,460
your dream to me.

5385
00:09:02,010 --> 00:09:03,650
Talk about cruel.

5386
00:09:04,890 --> 00:09:07,290
I'm being made to look into an old mirror.

5387
00:09:09,310 --> 00:09:11,920
There really was such a man once, wasn't there?

5388
00:09:27,690 --> 00:09:30,930
I've won, Archer.

5389
00:09:32,230 --> 00:09:35,750
Yes, and I've lost.

5390
00:09:47,950 --> 00:09:50,330
Shirou! Archer!

5391
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:57,140
Shirou, are you okay?

5392
00:09:57,140 --> 00:10:00,340
Archer, how did you get hurt like that?

5393
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:03,840
Sentimental to the core, I see.

5394
00:10:04,490 --> 00:10:10,390
If this girl had just been a little more callous, I never would have reverted to my old self.

5395
00:10:11,930 --> 00:10:14,540
In any case, the matter's been settled.

5396
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:20,590
Now that I've accepted you, the hero Emiya can no longer stay here.

5397
00:10:20,590 --> 00:10:23,200
The defeated should take their leave at once.

5398
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:24,110
Hey...

5399
00:10:29,730 --> 00:10:30,570
Archer!

5400
00:10:39,060 --> 00:10:41,290
That was most entertaining.

5401
00:10:41,290 --> 00:10:44,920
A truly pointless fight between two fakes.

5402
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,880
It can't be! You're...

5403
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:50,220
How long has it been, Saber? Ten years?

5404
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:56,680
So, do you finally comprehend the difference 
between your imitations and the genuine article?

5405
00:10:56,680 --> 00:11:02,200
No matter how closely you copy the shape or power, 
an imitation will never shine as brightly as the original.

5406
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:06,600
The mere sight of fakes crafted by fakes sullies my eyes.

5407
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,030
Scum.

5408
00:11:08,410 --> 00:11:14,290
Shams who do naught but copy others 
should return to the dust whence they came.

5409
00:11:24,090 --> 00:11:25,340
It's up to you...

5410
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:27,050
to defeat him.

5411
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,960
Archer!

5412
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:46,320
I'm surprised he had it in him to save another.

5413
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:49,400
Why, you...

5414
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:52,700
Who gave you permission to lay a hand on my Archer?

5415
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,730
I intended to start with that walking corpse,

5416
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:03,370
but I see the order has changed, woman.

5417
00:12:04,690 --> 00:12:06,390
Rin, stand back.

5418
00:12:07,070 --> 00:12:09,880
What are you doing here, Archer?

5419
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:12,930
Is it not obvious?

5420
00:12:12,930 --> 00:12:15,760
Following the conclusion of the previous War,

5421
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:18,970
I remained in this world instead of disappearing.

5424
00:12:19,610 --> 00:12:22,220
I had unfinished business, you see.

5425
00:12:23,090 --> 00:12:24,720
That's impossible.

5426
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:27,980
Servants should lose their anchor to this world

5427
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:29,980
the instant the Grail disappears.

5428
00:12:30,290 --> 00:12:34,300
You could not possibly have remained here for 10 years.

5429
00:12:34,300 --> 00:12:36,360
Not quite true.

5430
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:38,950
Even after the Grail has disappeared,

5431
00:12:38,950 --> 00:12:42,060
if a mage continues to supply us with mana,

5432
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:44,120
it is possible to remain here.

5433
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:46,800
Of course, without the Grails assistance,

5434
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,970
that means a vast amount of mana is required.

5435
00:12:49,970 --> 00:12:52,000
And to meet those needs...

5436
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:55,630
Well, there are any number of methods.

5437
00:12:55,630 --> 00:12:57,510
You can't seriously mean, your Master...

5438
00:12:57,510 --> 00:12:59,260
fed you human souls?!

5439
00:12:59,590 --> 00:13:00,510
Indeed.

5440
00:13:01,010 --> 00:13:05,700
It is the way of the world to steal from others
what one cannot provide for oneself.

5441
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,400
To be honest, though,

5442
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:10,270
it was not necessary to go to such lengths.

5443
00:13:10,930 --> 00:13:14,480
As the only Servant who bathed in the Grail,

5444
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:20,030
I took physical form in this era ten years ago.

5445
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:23,780
Yes, I have you to thank, Saber.

5446
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:29,400
I know its true nature better than anyone.

5447
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:34,790
As its innards poured out upon me, I saw what lay within it.

5448
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:37,250
In that instant, I made a decision:

5449
00:13:38,090 --> 00:13:40,920
that none but I would wield it.

5450
00:13:41,410 --> 00:13:43,670
Wield the Grail? You?

5451
00:13:43,670 --> 00:13:45,270
But of course.

5452
00:13:45,270 --> 00:13:49,350
The ritual to summon the Grail is a twisted joke.

5453
00:13:49,350 --> 00:13:52,760
A life-or-death struggle among seven Masters?

5454
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:57,430
A ritual wherein only the last Master standing wins the Grail?

5455
00:13:57,430 --> 00:13:59,940
That is but a pretext.

5456
00:14:00,430 --> 00:14:03,690
The Grail has been here the whole time.

5457
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:07,280
Each time, the mages first prepare the Grail,

5458
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:10,050
and then summon seven Servants.

5459
00:14:10,050 --> 00:14:11,970
Do you see, King of Knights?

5460
00:14:11,970 --> 00:14:17,240
What they wanted was not the Grail but its contents.

5461
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:22,540
While those mages did indeed create the Grail,

5462
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:25,200
they were unable to fill it.

5463
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:28,970
And so, they summoned the contents—

5464
00:14:29,650 --> 00:14:32,030
deceiving not only the Masters

5465
00:14:32,030 --> 00:14:34,670
but also their Servants.

5466
00:14:36,350 --> 00:14:39,760
You're quick on the uptake, Tohsaka wench.

5467
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:40,480
You are correct.

5468
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:44,640
The Grail must be filled with mana of the highest purity.

5469
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:48,850
And so, humanity's mightiest souls—its guardians, one might say—

5470
00:14:48,850 --> 00:14:52,040
were the very contents they sought!

5471
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:57,830
Th-That's not...

5472
00:14:57,830 --> 00:14:59,380
That's not possible!

5473
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:03,040
The more sacrifices, the better.

5474
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:06,160
If the souls of six Servants were fed into it,

5475
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:08,510
it would be nigh omnipotent.

5476
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:14,060
After all, to the mages, it would be a source of inexhaustible mana.

5477
00:15:14,550 --> 00:15:15,840
But then...

5478
00:15:16,590 --> 00:15:21,010
Then only a Master can wield the Grail.

5479
00:15:21,010 --> 00:15:24,270
If, as you say, the Grail is a repository of pure mana,

5480
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,650
then only a mage can use it.

5481
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:35,930
But I have no interest in such things.

5482
00:15:35,930 --> 00:15:39,540
Only in the Grail's ability to act as a hole.

5483
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:42,230
The Grail is a hole?

5484
00:15:43,470 --> 00:15:46,130
Think back ten years, Saber.

5485
00:15:58,380 --> 00:16:01,920
When I was but a step away from claiming the Grail,

5486
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:03,770
I was stopped by you.

5487
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:08,740
The Grail was cut in two by a holy sword.

5488
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:09,900
No way...

5489
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:11,820
Saber, you destroyed the Grail?

5490
00:16:12,410 --> 00:16:16,950
What spilled forth became a great inferno that seared the city.

5491
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:31,130
I was directly beneath it, so naturally, 
my body was drenched in the deluge.

5492
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:36,480
In that moment, I learned the Grail's real nature.

5493
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:39,150
In truth, it is a joke.

5494
00:16:39,150 --> 00:16:41,460
But even so, it has its uses.

5495
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:46,060
Of all the weapons in the world, 
there is none so perfectly tailored to killing.

5496
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:48,590
A weapon?

5497
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:53,910
You say that the Grail, something brought into being by Servants, is a weapon?

5498
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:57,020
By our nature, we ourselves are weapons.

5499
00:16:57,760 --> 00:17:00,910
The Grail merely takes that nature to its logical conclusion.

5500
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:04,160
The Holy Grail is a gateway to Hell.

5501
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:08,080
When it is opened, billions of curses will pour out.

5502
00:17:08,970 --> 00:17:11,670
Did Kotomine not tell you?

5503
00:17:12,110 --> 00:17:15,150
That it was a Grail that had already been corrupted?

5504
00:17:15,150 --> 00:17:19,930
A chalice of greed that you humans dragged down to Earth?

5505
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:23,730
That it is one of humanity's great evils,

5506
00:17:23,730 --> 00:17:26,310
tailored to cursing and killing humans?

5507
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:30,820
Then what you are after is humanity's...

5508
00:17:32,390 --> 00:17:36,820
Yes, the eradication of all humans in this era.

5509
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:45,240
This world is enjoyable, but it is also beyond redemption.

5510
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:50,460
A plenitude of mongrels enjoying life is an affront to the king.

5511
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:54,930
Wh-What do you mean, an affront to the king?

5512
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:59,560
What's the point of being king with no one to rule over?

5513
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:02,350
If they die out, so be it.

5514
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:08,110
Those who vanish as a consequence of 
their own sin cannot possibly be of value.

5515
00:18:08,770 --> 00:18:11,860
It is not mongrels that I desire.

5516
00:18:12,380 --> 00:18:16,800
It is those who can survive, even in the fires of Hell,

5517
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:19,490
who are worthy of my rule.

5518
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:23,360
In that respect, those who died last time were failures.

5519
00:18:24,810 --> 00:18:27,620
If a little fire like that is enough to kill them,

5520
00:18:28,230 --> 00:18:30,750
the humans of this time are far too frail.

5521
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:40,100
I do not know what those who created the Grail intended,

5522
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:42,850
but it is a convenient tool.

5523
00:18:43,530 --> 00:18:47,600
A death sentence that will fall equally on all humans.

5524
00:18:48,230 --> 00:18:52,770
A fathomless darkness, created by man, that kills only man.

5525
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:59,620
A hound worthy of being delegated this task of mine.

5526
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:05,600
So let us pick up where we left off ten years ago.

5527
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:08,370
Back then, a filthy mongrel interrupted us,

5528
00:19:08,910 --> 00:19:11,350
but now, there is no such mongrel present.

5529
00:19:12,190 --> 00:19:17,670
Admittedly, an even more inferior fake is in our presence.

5530
00:19:21,070 --> 00:19:22,190
It's up to you...

5531
00:19:23,330 --> 00:19:24,170
to defeat him.

5532
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:28,100
Why did he say that?

5533
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,990
Well, no matter.

5534
00:19:46,190 --> 00:19:48,580
I have slain my true target.

5535
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,820
That shall be enough for today.

5536
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:53,380
After all, I've collected a troubling amount of soot.

5537
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:56,920
Take heed: your lives are worth less to me than soot.

5538
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,920
You have no time to waste, however.

5539
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:04,680
I shall produce the Grail right away and open a hole leading to Hell.

5540
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:09,180
Saber, if you wish to recover it, act swiftly.

5541
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:14,310
This time, the Grail is a hasty affair, riddled with defects.

5542
00:20:15,290 --> 00:20:17,190
Be quick about it,

5543
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:21,120
or its contents will drain out completely.

5544
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:36,850
Goddamn it!

5545
00:20:37,610 --> 00:20:40,450
Everyone keeps getting in my way!

5546
00:20:42,790 --> 00:20:43,800
You!

5547
00:20:45,330 --> 00:20:47,390
You were wounded in battle?

5548
00:20:47,390 --> 00:20:49,140
I see you have joined the fray, Shinji.

5549
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:53,400
Whose fault do you think that is?

5550
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:57,880
I got stabbed by Lancer thanks to your incompetence!

5551
00:20:57,880 --> 00:21:01,390
So that is why that girl was still alive.

5552
00:21:02,150 --> 00:21:03,530
What of Kotomine?

5553
00:21:03,530 --> 00:21:06,150
Dead and gone!

5554
00:21:06,150 --> 00:21:10,790
Tohsaka slipped through my fingers because you and that priest are such worthless scum!

5555
00:21:12,010 --> 00:21:13,670
I see.

5556
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:16,320
That is a pity.

5557
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:18,130
You bet your ass it is!

5558
00:21:18,130 --> 00:21:22,170
Didn't you say that we couldn't get the Grail without Tohsaka?

5559
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:27,570
Calm yourself.

5560
00:21:27,570 --> 00:21:29,340
I can produce the Grail.

5561
00:21:30,510 --> 00:21:32,110
Produce it how?

5562
00:21:32,110 --> 00:21:37,790
The priest said that even if you have the Grail, you need a vessel.

5563
00:21:38,470 --> 00:21:42,650
He said it wouldn't work unless you had someone for a sacrifice!

5564
00:21:42,910 --> 00:21:44,510
That won't be an issue.

5565
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:49,910
We have another Master right here who can serve as a vessel, correct?

5567
00:22:01,220 --> 00:22:03,220
You desire the Grail, do you not?

5568
00:22:03,990 --> 00:22:05,500
Then I shall give it to you.

5569
00:22:06,220 --> 00:22:09,680
One should keep one's prized possessions close by at all times.

5570
00:22:15,470 --> 00:22:17,620
How unsightly.

5571
00:22:17,620 --> 00:22:21,570
Still, something ugly should best bring out the flavor.

5572
00:22:21,570 --> 00:22:26,080
And most of all, a man of your character should belch forth fine mud indeed.

5573
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,570
Right, Shinji?

5574
00:22:27,570 --> 00:22:30,860
It hurts... It hurts... It hurts!

5575
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:33,830
It's spreading... It's spreading!

5576
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:38,840
Help me... Help me!

5580
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:58,860
If I am destined to turn to ash and bones

